[segmented] whole · 8.277803917 seconds: Good morning everyone. Before we get into the numbers, I want to thank the support team for a remarkable quarter. They answered more tickets than ever before, and our satisfaction scores went up at the same time. That is not an accident, it comes from the training sessions we started in the spring, and from the new routing rules. We will keep both, and next month we will add a weekly review of the hardest cases, so that everyone learns from them. I also want to welcome the four people who joined us this quarter. Some of you have met them already. If you have not, please find a moment this week to say hello, and show them how we work. The second thing I want to cover is the launch plan for the autumn release, which moves the beta to the first week of October and the public release to the middle of November and gives the design team two extra weeks to finish the onboarding flow and the new setting screens while engineering focuses on performance and the long list of small fixes that customers keep asking about in every survey we send. Finally, Birdtown Flow will be part of the release, and we will dictate the release notes with it as a test. If it does well, we will use it for the documentation too. The budget for next year is due at the end of the month. Every team lead should have the template by now, please keep the estimates honest, and tell me early if something is likely to slip, because surprises in December help nobody, we have a lot to be proud of, and a lot still to do, please send me your questions before Friday, and I will answer them at the next meeting. Thank you all for listening, and have a great week.
